.nh
.TH "PB-SEND" "1" "Sep 2026" "Paperboat" "Paperboat CLI"

.SH NAME
pb-send - Send files to a machine's Paperboat Inbox


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBpb send <path>\&... --to <machine> [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Send files to a machine's Paperboat Inbox

.PP
Send one or more paths to the selected machine's Inbox. The command succeeds only after receiver verification and a durable receipt; --session associates the transfer with a terminal session.

.PP
JSON output is supported with --json.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for send

.PP
\fB--json\fP[=false]
	print JSON

.PP
\fB--session\fP=""
	terminal session ID for destination context

.PP
\fB--to\fP=""
	destination machine name or ID


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--config\fP=""
	path to the CLI config file

.PP
\fB--no-customization\fP[=false]
	ignore local shortcuts, command defaults, and TUI preferences

.PP
\fB--server\fP=""
	paperboat-server base URL override

.PP
\fB--workspace\fP=""
	resource workspace selector: personal or a team slug


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBpb(1)\fP, \fBpb-send-cancel(1)\fP, \fBpb-send-destination(1)\fP, \fBpb-send-list(1)\fP, \fBpb-send-status(1)\fP
